From 5a2940f1e4aeaee554de7f83f4d94a643343d602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trust-Worthy <jondeveloper0@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:42:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_ocb.c: handle
 AAD in EVP_Cipher()

EVP_Cipher() takes AAD as input with a NULL output.  The AES-OCB
one-shot function had no case for this, so the AAD was encrypted
as payload and written to the NULL output, which crashed the caller.

Pass a NULL output to the same code Update uses for AAD.  EVP_Cipher()
then gives the same ciphertext and tag as Update and Final.  The other
AEADs already handle a NULL output this way.

Fixes: 3837c202b5e9 "Add aes_ocb cipher to providers"
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Billy Bob Brumley <bbb@iki.fi>
Merge-date: Sun Nov 22 15:26:44 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33312
(cherry picked from commit 78b1eabec7ee25e38a31517c2592d31077c951cf)
---
 providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_ocb.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_ocb.c b/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_ocb.c
index 433e026..30d2a39 100644
--- a/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_ocb.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_ocb.c
@@ -512,6 +512,10 @@ static int aes_ocb_cipher(void *vctx, unsigned char *out, size_t *outl,
     if (in == NULL)
         return aes_ocb_block_final(vctx, out, outl, outsize);
 
+    /* A NULL output passes AAD, as with Update */
+    if (out == NULL)
+        return aes_ocb_block_update(vctx, out, outl, outsize, in, inl);
+
     if (outsize < inl) {
         ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_PROV, PROV_R_OUTPUT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL);
         return 0;
-- 
